.TH NETWHY 1
.SH NAME
netwhy \- collect DNS, default-route, and proxy evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netwhy
--host HOST [--port PORT] [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolves a hostname or IP address and, on Linux, records the local default route
and configured proxy environment. Proxy credentials and URL paths are not
emitted. The command does not test remote reachability or infer firewall and
network-namespace policy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --host HOST
Hostname or IP address to resolve.
.TP
.B --port PORT
Optional port context from 1 through 65535.
.TP
.B --format json
Emit the versioned JSON report (the only supported format).
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 means name resolution failed; 2 invalid usage; 3 a partial evidence report;
and 4 a runtime failure.
